.TH LIBKECCAK_K12_FINAL 3 LIBKECCAK
.SH NAME
libkeccak_k12_final - absorb the customisation string and finish KT128 input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libkeccak/k12.h>

int libkeccak_k12_final(struct libkeccak_k12 *\fIctx\fP, const void *\fIcustom\fP, size_t \fIlength\fP);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lkeccak .
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR libkeccak_k12_final ()
function absorbs the
.I length
customisation bytes from
.IR custom ,
followed by the encoding of their length, and ends the input. Whether the
input is hashed as a single piece or as a tree is determined from the
combined length of the message, the customisation string and that length
encoding, so an empty customisation string still contributes its
one-byte encoding. A NULL
.I custom
pointer is accepted only when
.I length
is zero. The buffer is only borrowed for the call.
.PP
On success the context leaves the input-accepting phase: further update
and final calls fail and only
.BR libkeccak_k12_squeeze (3)
is accepted. If the call fails the context is unchanged and may be
retried.
.SH RETURN VALUES
The function returns 0 on success and -1 on error, including when
.I ctx
is NULL, when final has already succeeded, or when
.I custom
is NULL with a non-zero
.IR length .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libkeccak_k12_update (3),
.BR libkeccak_k12_squeeze (3),
.BR libkeccak_k12 (7)
